mill-utilitarianism-1.md:1: argue/negation: mill-utilitarianism-1.logic.r1 P5 (S6): the sentence says "no", but P5 denies nothing it speaks of: it reads "if the renunciation contributes worthily to increase the amount of happiness in the world, then the one who renounces is deserving of honour and admiration" [in 1 of 2 runs]
